  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/admin-name-missing  (ADMIN_NAME_MISSING)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > ADMIN_PASSWORD_MISSING 1`] = `
"✗ No password was given for the administrator.
  Why:  NEXTLY_ADMIN_PASSWORD is not set, and no password was typed at a prompt. The password is never taken from an argument.
  Next: Set NEXTLY_ADMIN_PASSWORD, or run this in a terminal to be asked.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/admin-password-missing  (ADMIN_PASSWORD_MISSING)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > ADMIN_PASSWORD_TOO_WEAK 1`] = `
"✗ That password is too weak, so nothing was created.
  Why:  Password must be at least 12 characters
  Next: Choose a password that meets each rule listed, then run \`nextly users:create-admin\` again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/admin-password-too-weak  (ADMIN_PASSWORD_TOO_WEAK)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > ADMIN_PASSWORDS_DIFFER 1`] = `
"✗ The two passwords differ, so nothing was created.
  Why:  The password is asked for twice, and the two answers must match.
  Next: Run \`nextly users:create-admin\` again and type the same password both times.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/admin-passwords-differ  (ADMIN_PASSWORDS_DIFFER)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BASELINE_LOCK_RELEASED 1`] = `
"✗ The migrate lock was released without adopting the database.
  Why:  Nothing was written.
  Next: Retry once no other schema operation is running.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/baseline-lock-released  (BASELINE_LOCK_RELEASED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BLOCK_MANIFEST_STALE 1`] = `
"✗ The committed block manifest does not match this config.
  Why:  /home/you/app/src/types/generated/blocks.manifest.json does not match this config.
  Next: Run \`nextly generate:manifest\` and commit the result.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/block-manifest-stale  (BLOCK_MANIFEST_STALE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BLOCK_MANIFEST_UNREADABLE 1`] = `
"✗ The block manifest at /home/you/app/src/types/generated/blocks.manifest.json could not be read.
  Why:  EACCES: permission denied, open '/home/you/app/src/types/generated/blocks.manifest.json'
  Next: Check that the file can be read, or remove it and run \`nextly generate:manifest\` to write it again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/block-manifest-unreadable  (BLOCK_MANIFEST_UNREADABLE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BLOCK_SCHEMA_DERIVATION_FAILED 1`] = `
"✗ The block document schema could not be derived, so it was not emitted.
  Why:  Object.prototype has been extended; zod's registry reads \`id\` off the object given to .meta(), so the emitted schema loses the node's fields and would describe a format that accepts malformed nodes.
  Next: Find the code that adds properties to \`Object.prototype\`, often a dependency, and remove it; \`--verbose\` shows where the schema was derived.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/block-schema-derivation-failed  (BLOCK_SCHEMA_DERIVATION_FAILED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BUILD_GENERATION_FAILED 1`] = `
"✗ File generation failed, so the build stopped.
  Why:  EACCES: permission denied, mkdir '/home/you/app/src/db/schemas/zod'
  Next: Check that the output folders in \`nextly.config.ts\` can be written to, then run \`nextly build\` again; \`--verbose\` shows where it failed.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/build-generation-failed  (BUILD_GENERATION_FAILED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BUILD_MIGRATIONS_NOT_APPLIED 1`] = `
"✗ Migration issues: 1 pending migration(s).
  Why:  Pending: 20261029_100000_add_posts
  Next: Run \`nextly migrate\` to apply pending migrations.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/build-migrations-not-applied  (BUILD_MIGRATIONS_NOT_APPLIED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BUILD_STRICT_WARNINGS 1`] = `
"✗ Build failed due to 1 warning (--strict mode).
  Why:  Collection "posts" field "author": relationship target "people" is not defined in this config.
  Next: Fix each warning listed, or run \`nextly build\` without \`--strict\` to let warnings pass.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/build-strict-warnings  (BUILD_STRICT_WARNINGS)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BUILDER_MIGRATION_SNAPSHOT_MISSING 1`] = `
"✗ nextly migrate does not apply a Schema Builder migration file with no snapshot.
  Why:  1761732000000_update_posts.sql was written by the Schema Builder and has no snapshot beside it (meta/1761732000000_update_posts.snapshot.json), so nothing says what the database should look like once it has run.
  Next: Replace it with the migration \`nextly migrate:create\` writes for that change: delete 1761732000000_update_posts.sql, run \`nextly migrate:create --name=<name>\`, and commit the .sql file and its snapshot.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/builder-migration-snapshot-missing  (BUILDER_MIGRATION_SNAPSHOT_MISSING)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > BUILDER_RELATION_TARGET_UNKNOWN 1`] = `
