exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_RENAME_TARGET_UNKNOWN 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" renames "review", which is not one of its contributed collections/singles/components.
  Why:  \`.rename()\` renames only the collections, singles and field groups the plugin itself contributes.
  Next: Remove "review" from the \`.rename()\` map in \`nextly.config.ts\`, or correct it to a slug the plugin contributes.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-rename-target-unknown  (PLUGIN_RENAME_TARGET_UNKNOWN)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_ROUTE_COLLISION 1`] = `
"✗ Duplicate route GET /feeds/rss contributed by feeds and syndication.
  Why:  Both patterns match the same requests with as many fixed segments each, so nothing decides which of them answers.
  Next: Change the path of one of the two routes, or configure only one of the two plugins in \`nextly.config.ts\`.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-route-collision  (PLUGIN_ROUTE_COLLISION)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_ROUTE_MOUNT_INVALID 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" declares route "/summary" with an unknown mount "global".
  Why:  A route is registered under the mount it declares and looked up under "plugin" or "root", so it would never match.
  Next: Set the route's \`mount\` to "plugin" or "root", or leave it out for "plugin".
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-route-mount-invalid  (PLUGIN_ROUTE_MOUNT_INVALID)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_ROUTE_OPTIONS_INVALID 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" route GET /summary declares an option that cannot apply.
  Why:  rawBody is only meaningful on a method with a body, not GET.
  Next: Correct the option named in the route's declaration in the plugin.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-route-options-invalid  (PLUGIN_ROUTE_OPTIONS_INVALID)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_ROUTE_PATH_INVALID 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" declares a route path "summary" that does not start with "/".
  Why:  A route's path is mounted under \`/plugins/<plugin>\`, so it must be absolute within that namespace.
  Next: Start the route's path with "/", as in "/summary".
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-route-path-invalid  (PLUGIN_ROUTE_PATH_INVALID)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_ROUTE_ROOT_UNREACHABLE 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" declares a root-mounted route at "/admin-meta/reviews", which cannot answer.
  Why:  The admin metadata endpoints answer from the verb wrappers, and the GET branch claims the whole subtree, so the fallback this route waits for is never reached.
  Next: Leave the route under the plugin's namespace (\`mount: "plugin"\`), or move it to a path whose first segment no built-in handler claims.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-route-root-unreachable  (PLUGIN_ROUTE_ROOT_UNREACHABLE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SCHEMA_BEHIND 1`] = `
"✗ The plugin "@acme/seo" expects schema version 3, and the database has 2.
  Why:  The applied version is the newest \`schemaVersion\` among the plugin's migrations recorded as applied, and production does not start a plugin ahead of its tables.
