  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-schema-behind  (PLUGIN_SCHEMA_BEHIND)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SCHEMA_VERSION_INVALID 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares schemaVersion 0.
  Why:  It must be a positive integer.
  Next: Set the plugin's \`schemaVersion\` to a positive integer, such as \`1\`, or install a release of the plugin that does.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-schema-version-invalid  (PLUGIN_SCHEMA_VERSION_INVALID)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SCHEMA_VERSION_NOT_ADVANCED 1`] = `
"✗ The plugin's schemaVersion must move past 3 before new migrations can be generated (it is 3).
  Why:  The runner takes a plugin's schema version from its last migration, so a new migration that changes the schema must declare a higher one.
  Next: Raise \`schemaVersion\` in \`@acme/seo\` above 3, then generate the migration again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-schema-version-not-advanced  (PLUGIN_SCHEMA_VERSION_NOT_ADVANCED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_DUPLICATE 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares the secret path "apiKey" twice.
  Why:  Each setting is encrypted once, so each path is listed once.
  Next: Remove the second "apiKey" from \`capabilities.secrets\`.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secret-path-duplicate  (PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_DUPLICATE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_EMPTY 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares an empty secret path.
  Why:  Each entry in \`capabilities.secrets\` names a setting by its dotted path in \`contributes.settings\`.
  Next: Remove the empty entry from \`capabilities.secrets\`, or write the path of the setting it is for.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secret-path-empty  (PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_EMPTY)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_NAMES_GROUP 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares the secret path "provider", which names a group of settings rather than one value.
  Why:  A secret is one stored value, so its path ends at a single setting.
  Next: Name the value inside it.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secret-path-names-group  (PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_NAMES_GROUP)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_NOT_STRING 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares the secret path "retries", which names a value that cannot be a string.
  Why:  A secret is stored as a string.
  Next: Point "retries" at a text setting, or make the setting it names a string.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secret-path-not-string  (PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_NOT_STRING)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_UNKNOWN 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares the secret path "apiKey", which its settings schema does not contain.
  Why:  A secret path the schema does not have would leave the credential it is for stored in plain text.
  Next: Correct "apiKey" to the path of a setting in \`contributes.settings\`, or add that setting.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secret-path-unknown  (PLUGIN_SECRET_PATH_UNKNOWN)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SECRETS_WITHOUT_SETTINGS 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares secret paths but no settings schema (contributes.settings) for them to name.
  Why:  A secret path names a setting to encrypt, so without \`contributes.settings\` it names nothing.
  Next: Add the settings schema under \`contributes.settings\`, or remove \`capabilities.secrets\`.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-secrets-without-settings  (PLUGIN_SECRETS_WITHOUT_SETTINGS)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SETTINGS_KEY_TOO_LONG 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reports" declares the settings key "deliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydelivery", which is longer than the 191 characters the settings storage holds.
  Why:  Settings are stored by key, in a column of that width.
  Next: Shorten "deliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydeliverydelivery" to 191 characters or fewer.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-settings-key-too-long  (PLUGIN_SETTINGS_KEY_TOO_LONG)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SETTINGS_PERMISSION_UNDECLARED 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" declares settingsPermission "manage-reviews", which is not one of its own permissions (moderate-reviews).
  Why:  \`settingsPermission\` must name a permission the plugin declares itself, so that a role can be given it.
  Next: Declare "manage-reviews" among the plugin's own permissions, or set \`settingsPermission\` to one it already declares.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-settings-permission-undeclared  (PLUGIN_SETTINGS_PERMISSION_UNDECLARED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SETTINGS_PERMISSION_WITHOUT_SETTINGS 1`] = `
"✗ Plugin "reviews" declares settingsPermission "manage-reviews" but no settings schema for it to guard.
  Why:  \`settingsPermission\` guards the plugin's settings, and the plugin declares no \`contributes.settings\`.
  Next: Add the settings schema under \`contributes.settings\`, or remove \`settingsPermission\`.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/plugin-settings-permission-without-settings  (PLUGIN_SETTINGS_PERMISSION_WITHOUT_SETTINGS)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > PLUGIN_SETUP_FAILED 1`] = `
"✗ The \`@nextlyhq/plugin-seo\` plugin failed while the configuration was loading.
