  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/resolve-snapshot-missing  (RESOLVE_SNAPSHOT_MISSING)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SCHEMA_CHANGE_WITHOUT_MIGRATION 1`] = `
"✗ 2 pending schema change(s) detected.
  Why:  + add_column dc_posts.subtitle (text)
        + add_table dc_authors
  Next: Run \`nextly migrate:create --name="<migration-name>"\` and commit the result.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/schema-change-without-migration  (SCHEMA_CHANGE_WITHOUT_MIGRATION)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SCHEMA_LOCK_HELD 1`] = `
"✗ \`nextly migrate\` did not start, and changed nothing: the schema lock is still held after waiting 30 s.
  Why:  \`nextly db:sync\` holds it (process 4242 on build-01, started 2 min ago at 2026-10-29T10:00:00Z). If that process has stopped, the lock lapses in 30 s, at 2026-10-29T10:02:30Z, with nobody clearing it by hand.
  Next: Run it again once that finishes.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/schema-lock-held  (SCHEMA_LOCK_HELD)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SCHEMA_LOCK_LOST 1`] = `
"✗ db:sync finished, but could not keep the schema lock to the end.
  Why:  Another run took it while the work ran.
  Next: Check the database before running it again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/schema-lock-lost  (SCHEMA_LOCK_LOST)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SCHEMA_LOCK_UNAVAILABLE 1`] = `
"✗ The command did not run: the schema lock could not be taken.
  Why:  Its row in \`nextly_schema_lock\` could not be established, and running without the lock would leave other runs free to change the schema at the same time.
  Next: Check that the database user can create and write that table, then run the command again; \`--verbose\` shows the details.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/schema-lock-unavailable  (SCHEMA_LOCK_UNAVAILABLE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SCHEMA_SYNC_IN_PRODUCTION 1`] = `
"✗ Cannot auto-sync schema in production mode.
  Why:  \`NODE_ENV\` is \`production\`, and 2 collections would change: posts, pages.
  Next: Run \`nextly migrate:create --name="<migration-name>"\` to create migrations, then \`nextly migrate\` to apply.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/schema-sync-in-production  (SCHEMA_SYNC_IN_PRODUCTION)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SETTINGS_CHANGE_WITHOUT_MIGRATION 1`] = `
"✗ 1 entity's settings changed with no migration.
  Why:  ~ posts: labels.singular
  Next: Run \`nextly migrate:create --name="<migration-name>"\` and commit the result.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/settings-change-without-migration  (SETTINGS_CHANGE_WITHOUT_MIGRATION)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SETUP_ALREADY_COMPLETE 1`] = `
"✗ Setup is already complete: this install has an administrator. Nothing was created.
  Why:  Only the first administrator is created here, and this install has one.
  Next: Sign in as that administrator, and add other accounts from the admin.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/setup-already-complete  (SETUP_ALREADY_COMPLETE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SETUP_IN_PROGRESS 1`] = `
"✗ A setup is in progress on this install, so the token was not replaced.
  Why:  One setup runs at a time, and another setup, from the web or this command, holds this install's setup claim.
  Next: Run \`nextly setup-token\` again in a moment.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/setup-in-progress  (SETUP_IN_PROGRESS)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SETUP_TOKEN_SET_BY_ENV 1`] = `
"✗ NEXTLY_SETUP_TOKEN sets this install's token, so there is no generated one to replace.
  Why:  A token set by NEXTLY_SETUP_TOKEN is read from the environment, not stored in the install's database.
  Next: Change the variable where it is set.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/setup-token-set-by-env  (SETUP_TOKEN_SET_BY_ENV)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SNAPSHOT_WITHOUT_MIGRATION 1`] = `
"✗ The snapshot \`20261020_120000_add_posts.snapshot.json\` exists but \`20261020_120000_add_posts.sql\` does not.
  Why:  A snapshot is written beside the migration it describes, and this one's migration was deleted or never committed.
  Next: Restore the .sql file from version control, or delete the orphan snapshot.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/snapshot-without-migration  (SNAPSHOT_WITHOUT_MIGRATION)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > SQLITE_FOREIGN_KEYS_STILL_ON 1`] = `
"✗ Foreign-key enforcement could not be switched off for this migration.
  Why:  Another transaction was open on the connection. Nothing was applied.
  Next: Re-run it once that transaction has finished.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/sqlite-foreign-keys-still-on  (SQLITE_FOREIGN_KEYS_STILL_ON)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UI_SCHEMA_INVALID 1`] = `
"✗ \`ui-schema.json\` failed validation.
  Why:  collections.0.slug: slug must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$
  Next: Fix each entry listed in \`ui-schema.json\`, or make the change again in the Schema Builder, then run the command again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/ui-schema-invalid  (UI_SCHEMA_INVALID)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UI_SCHEMA_NOT_JSON 1`] = `
"✗ ui-schema.json is not valid JSON.
  Why:  Unexpected token '}', "{ "collections": [ }" is not valid JSON
  Next: Fix the JSON at the position named, or restore \`ui-schema.json\` from version control, then run the command again.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/ui-schema-not-json  (UI_SCHEMA_NOT_JSON)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UI_SCHEMA_UNREADABLE 1`] = `
"✗ Failed to read ui-schema file at /home/you/app/ui-schema.json.
  Why:  EACCES: permission denied, open '/home/you/app/ui-schema.json'
  Next: Check that the file is readable by the user running the command, or point \`db.uiSchemaFile\` in \`nextly.config.ts\` at the right file.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/ui-schema-unreadable  (UI_SCHEMA_UNREADABLE)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UNEXPECTED_ERROR 1`] = `
"✗ The command stopped on an error Nextly did not expect.
  Why:  Failed query: no such column: localized
  Next: Run it again with \`--verbose\` to see the details, and report it at https://github.com/nextlyhq/nextly/issues if it keeps happening.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/unexpected-error  (UNEXPECTED_ERROR)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UPGRADE_BACKUP_NOT_CONFIRMED 1`] = `
"✗ Refusing to upgrade without a confirmed backup.
  Why:  No terminal is attached to ask whether the database is backed up, and \`--confirm-backed-up\` was not passed. Nothing was changed.
  Next: Re-run with \`--confirm-backed-up\` (CI/non-TTY) after backing up your database.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/upgrade-backup-not-confirmed  (UPGRADE_BACKUP_NOT_CONFIRMED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UPGRADE_CANCELLED 1`] = `
"✗ Upgrade cancelled by operator.
  Why:  The upgrade asks for a backup before its first step that changes anything, and the answer was no. Nothing was changed.
  Next: Back up the database, then run \`nextly upgrade\` again and answer yes.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/upgrade-cancelled  (UPGRADE_CANCELLED)"
`;

exports[`each code, as a command ends with it > UPGRADE_EVENTS_TABLE_TAKEN 1`] = `
"✗ A table named "nextly_schema_events" already exists with an unexpected shape.
  Why:  \`nextly upgrade\` moves the migration records into "nextly_schema_events", and the table there does not have the columns it writes. Nothing was changed.
  Next: Rename it, or re-run with \`--target-table-name <name>\`.
  Docs: https://nextlyhq.com/docs/cli/errors/upgrade-events-table-taken  (UPGRADE_EVENTS_TABLE_TAKEN)"
`;
